From 78713dd14046285b30656e34d4d7ee73c06fef61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dong Chenchen <superdcc97@163.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 20:58:40 +0800
Subject: [RFC PATCH 1/3] bpf, sockmap: Pin the psock owning the backlog work

sk_psock_backlog() gets its psock from the delayed work, but takes a
reference through the socket's current sk_user_data. After the initial
TX_ENABLED check, map deletion and reinsertion can replace that psock.
The worker then gets the replacement and puts its original work owner,
underflowing the old reference count and leaking the new reference.

Increment the work owner's reference count directly, unless it has
already reached zero. The destroy work synchronously cancels the backlog
before freeing that psock or dropping its socket reference, so this
attempt cannot access a freed psock. Retain the reference handshake with
sock_map_close() that keeps sk_socket alive while work is running.

Fixes: 8259eb0e06d8 ("bpf, sockmap: Avoid using sk_socket after free when sending")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dong Chenchen <superdcc97@163.com>
---
 net/core/skmsg.c | 10 +++++-----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/core/skmsg.c b/net/core/skmsg.c
index 2521b643fa05..2d2217a60313 100644
--- a/net/core/skmsg.c
+++ b/net/core/skmsg.c
@@ -685,12 +685,12 @@ static void sk_psock_backlog(struct work_struct *work)
 	if (!sk_psock_test_state(psock, SK_PSOCK_TX_ENABLED))
 		return;
 
-	/* Increment the psock refcnt to synchronize with close(fd) path in
-	 * sock_map_close(), ensuring we wait for backlog thread completion
-	 * before sk_socket freed. If refcnt increment fails, it indicates
-	 * sock_map_close() completed with sk_socket potentially already freed.
+	/*
+	 * Pin the work owner; sk_user_data may already contain a new psock.
+	 * Destroy synchronously cancels this work before freeing the old one.
+	 * A live reference also makes close wait before freeing sk_socket.
 	 */
-	if (!sk_psock_get(psock->sk))
+	if (!refcount_inc_not_zero(&psock->refcnt))
 		return;
 	mutex_lock(&psock->work_mutex);
 	while ((skb = skb_peek(&psock->ingress_skb))) {
-- 
